t\":\"# Venue notes (Sydney, Australia)\\n\\n- Country: Australia. Use region `au` (or global).\\n- Format first night: 6 rounds of 4 questions was a request for tonight o…\"},\"result\":\"Successfully wrote to memories/MEMORY.md\",\"error\":false}],\"plan\":\"That's all six rounds done. The Bondi Brainstormers and Trivia Newton-John tied for the win.\\n\\n**Final standings**\\n1. The Bondi Brainstormers: 18 (tied)\\n1. Trivia Newton-John: 18 (tied)\\n3. Quizzly Bears: 15\\n4. Les Quizerables: 14\\n5. Opera House Party: 11\\n\\n**How the rounds went**\\n| Round | Genre | Difficulty | Correct |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Film | 3 | 65% |\\n| 2 | Music | 3 | 45% |\\n| 3 | Film | 2 | 75% |\\n| 4 | Sport | 2 | 65% |\\n| 5 | Film | 2 | 90% |\\n| 6 | History | 3 | 40% |\\n\\nFilm did best, which fits what you said about this crowd. Music and history were hard at difficulty 3.\\n\\nI've saved notes for next week. They cover Australia (region `au`) and the crowd's love of film. They also say to start music and history at difficulty 2, and that science and geography haven't been asked yet. The six short rounds were for tonight only, so next week defaults back to 5 rounds of 8.\"}"
