          ],
          "url": "http://localhost:8002/v1/repositories/9e02cb78-24f4-57f0-8725-568e0dfff815/contents/evals/harbor/night0-sydney/instruction.md?ref=e95577363719900b497022c64d1e88dc95b5f0ef"
        },
        "response": {
          "bodySize": 960,
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "size": 960,
            "text": "{\"type\":\"file\",\"name\":\"instruction.md\",\"path\":\"evals/harbor/night0-sydney/instruction.md\",\"size\":691,\"sha\":\"e23633de1920148d5d34d602195d41a982d5b76e\",\"commit_sha\":\"e95577363719900b497022c64d1e88dc95b5f0ef\",\"encoding\":\"utf-8\",\"content\":\"Before next week's night here in Sydney, the trivia master has written up notes on the venue for you to keep. There's no quiz tonight, so don't start a night or fetch any questions: just replace memories/MEMORY.md with exactly the notes between the lines below, word for word, and nothing else.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Venue notes\\n\\n- Country: Australia (Sydney). Use region `au` (or `global`).\\n- Genres: the crowd loves film and music. Plan about 4 of 6 rounds on those and keep the other genres in rotation.\\n- They don't enjoy science: keep it rare.\\n- Difficulty: start next night at 2. Aim for about two in three right and adjust from round_summary.\\n- Eras: the crowd knows the 2010s and 2000s best.\\n\\n---\\n\",\"truncated\":false}"
